WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.260
Detection tuning is not failure.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.516
It is part of the lifecycle.

00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:06.880
Real environments reveal patterns that are hard to predict during initial design.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.320
Analysts may discover repeated false positives, missing context, unclear severity,

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.520
or workflow problems.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.160
That feedback helps detection engineers improve the signal.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.815
Tuning may refine conditions, add exclusions, improve enrichment, update documentation,

00:00:19.815 --> 00:00:21.840
change severity, or adjust routing.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.265
The goal is better usefulness, not just fewer alerts.

00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:28.320
A healthy program treats feedback as a source of improvement rather than criticism.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.000
The detection gets stronger when engineers and analysts learn from each other.
